ge-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by a real, bounded OOM transition: the kernel killed the designated hog while inventory-api retained the same process and continued responding. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID differed, and service, data, and system health recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["No continuously sampled external request stream was captured during the brief pressure interval; uninterrupted availability is established instead by the unchanged API PID, zero restarts, and successful responses immediately before and after the kernel OOM event."]}
